# M1 exit transcript (ARCHITECTURE §22.3, WP 1.26)

`vertical_slice.in/vertical_slice.py` holds the 19 statements of the M1 exit transcript, both
syntaxes mixed: clear the factory scene, add a cylinder, give it a metallic `Steel` material,
add a camera, render it with Workbench, export a GLB, save a `.frap`, start empty, import the
GLB back (its material is still metallic), reopen the `.frap` (the cylinder is where it was).
Output paths are cwd-relative (`out/…`, never `//`, §17.2); the sandbox starts empty.

The same statements run in the other two transports:

- `vertical_slice_stdin.toml`: raw mode, statements on stdin (§13.1);
- `vertical_slice_serve.toml`: `frap serve --jsonl`, one request per statement, so the session
  state crosses requests (§13.1, §13.5).

The exit transcript needs `object.camera_add` (WP 1.20), the IO operators (1.23) and
`render.render` (1.24); it was gated until those WPs merged in the M1 W4 integration.

Every statement must finish (`"ok":true`). Each round trip is proven by the statement that
performs it, not only by the value read afterwards: `wm.read_homefile` removes the cylinder
and the `Steel` material and leaves no active object; `import_scene.gltf` adds exactly the
`Cylinder` object, its mesh and `Steel` (so the `Metallic` of `1` read next comes from the
GLB); `wm.open_mainfile` adds the camera back and makes it active again, which only the saved
`.frap` can do (the GLB has no camera), so the cylinder read at `[0,0,1]` is the reopened one.
Details owned by the operator WPs (1.20, 1.23, 1.24: byte counts, absolute paths, the full
`changes` of the file operators) are elided with `[..]`; those WPs have their own goldens and
transcripts. The render needs a GPU adapter (Metal, lavapipe, WARP on the CI matrix).

The error-code and `poll()` sections run first, so that a failing exit transcript does not
hide them (trycmd skips the remaining steps of a file after a failure).

## Error codes (runs first)

The golden cases under `tests/golden/cases/{errors,rna,context,poll}/` compare every error's
exception class and message with Blender 5.2.4 (fixtures blessed from Blender); goldens do not
see frap's `code`. `vertical_slice.in/error_codes.py` raises each M1-reachable code once so
that the code, span, detail and hint are pinned too, including the frap-only codes Blender has
no counterpart for (`UNSUPPORTED_SYNTAX`, `OP_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`, `NOT_IMPLEMENTED`,
`OP_ARG_POSITIONAL` D-01, `ZERO_DIVISION` D-25, `RNA_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`, `LIMIT_EXCEEDED`).
`IO_ERROR` (line 26) is pinned here by class and code only; its message is pinned, and checked
against Blender, in the section at the end. `REQUEST_INVALID` and `DESCRIBE_TARGET` are
pinned by the WP 1.25 transcripts under `cli/`; `RNA_EDITMODE_WRITE` needs Edit Mode (M2);
`GPU_UNAVAILABLE` needs a build without `gpu`. (snapbox turns backslashes into `/`, so `\"` reads `/"` below.)

