## `bpy.ops.<op>.poll()` values

Golden line outcomes carry no values, so the poll goldens `tests/golden/cases/poll/*.py` pin
Blender's results with `#@blender assert … is True/False` lines (blessing fails if Blender
disagrees). `vertical_slice.in/poll_*.py` are byte-identical copies of those four cases; running
them through frap pins frap's `"value"` of every `poll()` line (`"kind":"op_meta"`), so a poll
that always answered `true` (or `false`) fails here. Every `"value"` below equals the
`#@blender assert` on the line after it in the case file. A failing poll answers `"ok":true`
with `"value":false` and the reason in `result` (Blender's `poll()` returns `False`, it does
not raise).

```console
$ frap run --no-ready --verbosity minimal poll_factory.py
