## Operator errors and polls of WP 1.20, 1.23, 1.24

`IO_ERROR` and the real `OP_EXEC_ERROR` (a `RuntimeError` raised by `execute`, not the
`TypeError` of the dynamic `mode_set` enum above) need the IO operators and the render
operator. The messages of `import_scene.gltf(filepath='missing.glb')` (`Error: Please select a
file`), `wm.open_mainfile` of a missing file (`Error: Cannot read file "<abs path>": No such
file or directory`) and `render.render()` without a camera (`Error: Cannot render, no camera`)
were checked against Blender 5.2.4 (cd5dc428cce1): class and message are identical.
`export_scene.gltf(filepath='')` differs: Blender raises `RuntimeError` with the add-on's whole
Python traceback (`Error: Python: Traceback (most recent call last): … FileNotFoundError:
[Errno 2] No such file or directory: ''`); frap keeps the last line only. That difference has
no deviations.md entry yet (WP 1.23 or the integrator). The error-code block above elides this
message because it changes when WP 1.23 lands (`Error: filepath not set` before).

`ops_polls.py` pins `poll()` of the operators WP 1.20, 1.23 and 1.24 add, in the factory scene,
with no active object, with nothing selected, and with a camera active; each value was checked
against Blender 5.2.4 by running the same script there.

